Claim type: bounded_theorem

A fixed polynomial Lie-certificate family permits selecting a positive coupling at each desired accuracy. The selected coupling controls both the compiler conditioning and the drift during a finite output window. This gives explicit sufficient polynomial upper recipes in inverse tolerance for a fixed complete plant and fixed certificate. It does not give polynomial scaling in qubit count, useful numerical constants, a native controller or a device implementation.

Primary-runner role: source integrity only. The proposed 60-second primary checks exact bodies, recovery intervals, canonical-parent identities and actual root binding evidence. It runs no determinant example, coefficient-grid search, recurrence search, pulse simulation, scientific fixture or proof test. The historical source proposal remains unexecuted. Current binding separately captures actual root publication review f09815c0befcc6fb80aa0a98a59383d3a37bed5d5b6031bbcc044f9a7a16b9b0 and selected Git base PR 9622; future primary/cache/action outcomes are not inferred. Source assembly and metadata counts are not independent mathematical evidence.

Actual qualified source acceptance is `e0735ca8d982440594af54e9d711071531d40042440fc26b1f7e131677747ade`, recorded at 21:15:19.600585–21:15:19.689261 UTC on 2026-10-15 by the captured root metadata operation, exit 0. It accepts the original construction and separately attributed sharpening under consistent computable coordinate data, the stated fixed-family premises and a shared integrated defect budget. That source decision is distinct from the actual wrapper acceptance f09815c0befcc6fb80aa0a98a59383d3a37bed5d5b6031bbcc044f9a7a16b9b0, future publication and independent retained status. Its exact review, freeze and real source-at-launch/stream evidence are recoverable in the packet.

Three immutable bodies follow: the original root construction `6cae05fe…`, its separate sharpening readout `899a28b9…`, and source-exposed assessment `c9c09872…`. The original construction uses the degree-bound exponent `D`; the `k0` refinement belongs to the separate root readout. The explicit uniform constants below belong to the exposed assessment. No protected independent derivation of this interpolation route is claimed. Historical pending statements remain literal in all three bodies.

## 1. Fixed supplied interface and actual complete target

Fix a nonempty complete finite plant of dimension `d>=2`, including all original data, apparatus, memory, clock factors and dirty fillers, with an arbitrary correlated passive reference. Supply the full computable nominal onsite/ordinary-NN background `H`, including literal original `H0`, its full bound `h>=||H||`, a positive ordinary-NN path Hamiltonian `J`, one accessible X/Y control port, `g>0`, and a fixed time unit `t0>0`. No old factor moves, is initialized or is discarded. The path may add interactions on existing old edges; it does not create a spare physical neighbor at a saturated site. Its complete box/filler geometry and all omitted/exterior couplings remain governed by the sole compiler parent.

Write `H=h0 I+Hbar`, `J=j0 I+Jbar`. For a full target unitary `W` supply computable target entries and a determinant lift `theta` with `W=exp(i theta) Wtilde`. The nominal physical Hamiltonian is

```
H_ph(t)=H+R_s I+lambda J+C(t),
C(t)=g f(t)(I+sign P_p)>=0,   P_p in {X_p,Y_p},   0<=f<=1.
```

At most one pulse is active. Cubic ramps make its value and derivative vanish at segment endpoints; the port is zero during the final window. `R_s>=h` gives whole nominal positivity. It does not imply separately positive old local blocks. The path, port controls, isolation, timing and finite coefficient precision are supplied physical premises.

The complete comparator for the compiler's actual returned duration `T` and `0<=s<=w` is

```
V_s=exp[-i chi(T+s)] exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH),
chi(T+s)=(R_s+lambda j0)(T+s)+A_s+theta,
A_s=integral_0^T g f(t)dt.
```

The full unchanged `H` ages the input before the ideal target and acts after it during the window. In general this is not `W exp[-i(T+s)H]`. The scalar `h0` is already in those `H` flows. `theta` is a comparison-phase lift, not applied scalar Hamiltonian action. Every recurrence wait contributes its actual time and phase. There is no assumption that `lambda T` is small and no prescribed completion deadline. Design/search occurs before the declared physical timeline; any plant evolution during design needs a separate chronological contract.

## 2. Fixed computable polynomial certificate

Define five full augmented skew-Hermitian matrices

```
X_i(z)=diag(-i t0[Hbar+z Jbar+v_i], -i t0 Hbar),
v_i in {0,+gX_p,-gX_p,+gY_p,-gY_p},        0<=z<=1.
```

The direct sum is mathematical bookkeeping, not another physical plant. Fix `s_0=d^2-1` binary bracket trees with leaf counts `ell_l>=2`; their evaluations are `diag(b_l(z),0)`. The zero second block is exact because all second leaf blocks coincide. In a fixed **computable** real Hilbert-Schmidt orthonormal basis of `su(d)`, let `C(z)` contain the coordinates of the `b_l(z)`. Equivalently, supply consistent computable polynomial coordinates. An arbitrary noncomputable basis would not justify finite computable searches.

Every column has degree at most `ell_l`. Thus

```
p(z)=det C(z)=sum_(k=0)^D a_k z^k,     D=sum_l ell_l
```

has the displayed degree upper bound, which need not be its exact degree or order of vanishing. Supply one index `k0 in {0,...,D}` and rational `a>0` with `abs(a_k0)>=a`. This fixes a nonidentically-zero determinant for this same tree family across the whole accuracy family. No lower coefficient is declared zero; `k0` need not be the first nonzero index. Obtaining this certificate or a suitable tree list is a separate operation. A certified nonzero determinant at a rational point for the same family permits a terminating coefficient-enclosure search without deciding zeros, but supplies no uniform discovery or oracle-time bound.

Supply rational `M>=1` bounding every full `X_i(z)` uniformly, and put

```
beta_l=2^(ell_l-1) M^ell_l,
Bsum=sum_l beta_l,     ell=max_l ell_l,
U>=sqrt(d) Bsum,       U positive rational.
```

The bracket norm inequality gives `norm(b_l(z))<=beta_l`; Hilbert-Schmidt coordinates then give `norm(C(z))_2<=U`. These are complete-plant bounds, not projected or excitation-sector estimates. All certificate data, `H,J,g,t0,d`, the target access and the finite window remain fixed as tolerance varies.

## 3. Selected finite coupling grid and two exponent choices

Use exactly the `D+1` rational nodes

```
x_j=1/2+j/[2(D+1)],        j=0,...,D,
V_(j,k)=x_j^k,
A_V=sum_j abs((V^-1)_(k0,j))>0.
```

Lagrange interpolation, equivalently coefficient extraction by `V^-1`, gives

```
max_j abs(p(Lambda x_j)) >= a Lambda^k0/A_V,   0<Lambda<=1.
```

For the original construction set `nu=D`. For the separately attributed sharpening set `nu=k0`. In either case define `b=a Lambda^nu/A_V`; approximate each grid value with certified absolute error at most `b/8` and accept a node when `abs(p_hat_j)-b/8>b/2`. A witness has lower estimate at least `3b/4`, so the finite strict test terminates without threshold refinement or exact-zero decisions. The selected actual rational coupling satisfies

```
Lambda/2<=lambda<Lambda,
abs(det C(lambda))>a Lambda^nu/(2A_V).
```

Choose a fixed rational majorant `K_cert` as below. The singular-value product bound yields

```
sigma_min(C(lambda))>a Lambda^nu/[2 A_V U^(s_0-1)],
kappa(Lambda)=K_cert Lambda^-nu,
K_cert>=max(1,2 sqrt(s_0 d) A_V U^(s_0-1)/a),
sum_l abs(c_l)<=kappa(Lambda) norm(sum_l c_l b_l(lambda)).
```

This supplies the parent's quantitative full augmented-basis premise at the **selected** coupling. It does not establish the premise at every small coupling. `D` still sets the node count and Vandermonde constants in the `k0` version; replacing the grid by `k0+1` nodes would be unjustified. `k0=0` is allowed only when that coefficient is actually certified. No coupling, target or recurrence search has been executed for this packet.

## 4. Finite-window accuracy and one total defect allowance

For any rational desired complete unhalved trace tolerance `0<epsilon<=1`, supply rational `b_bar>=||Jbar||`, `w_bar>=w`, and fixed positive rational

```
L_win>=max(1,64 b_bar(1+w_bar)),
Lambda=epsilon/L_win,                   0<epsilon<=1.
```

Select `lambda` from the finite grid and use the protected finite-target-grid compiler recipe at tolerance `eta=epsilon`, with the actual selected matrices, same trees and `kappa(Lambda)`. This is that particular parent recipe, not an identification with its different supplied-logarithm/rational-duration recipe. The inherited smoothed coherent endpoint error is at most `15epsilon/32`. During the final window the actual static path gives at most `lambda||Jbar||w<=epsilon/64` additional coherent error. It is retained throughout the preceding compilation interval.

Let `E_int=integral_0^(T+w)||H_actual(t)-H_nominal(t)||dt` use the full retained Hilbert space. With `E_int<=epsilon/64`, the complete unhalved trace error for every plant/reference input is at most

```
2[15epsilon/32+epsilon/64+epsilon/64]=epsilon.
```

All simultaneous calibration, timing, coefficient, scalar, old-background and omitted-edge errors share this **one total** integrated allowance. Each cannot spend the full allowance independently. An input-state error adds once by contractivity and needs its own allocation if the final total is to remain `epsilon`. No marginal conditioning or output discard is used. A memory/reset consumer must impose its premise on the actually aged input; an initial purity promise is not automatically preserved by a long compiler.

## 5. Explicit sufficient resources and their attribution

The following uniform majorants are the exposed assessment's rederivation. They are not part of an independent pre-exposure result. Set

```
kappa_0=K_cert L_win^nu,
K_bar=1+s_0[4 kappa_0(d+1)+2],      S_bar=K_bar Bsum,
a_l^rem=(k_l M)^(ell_l+1)/(ell_l+1)!+beta_l^2/2,
C_bar=2 K_bar^2 sum_l a_l^rem,      Q_word=2 sum_l k_l,
R=ell(2nu+1),                      P=R+2d(R+1),
C_r=1+2K_bar+8S_bar^2+(16C_bar)^ell,
C_N=Q_word C_r,                    C_Q=1+512(2d)C_N,
C_T=2t0 C_N C_Q^(2d),              C_rho=8C_r/t0+16gC_N.
```

Here `k_l` is the parent's signed-word length; `a_l^rem` is a Taylor remainder bound, distinct from determinant coefficients `a_k`. Use the parent's specified sufficient count

```
r=ceil max{1,2K,8S^2/epsilon,(16C/epsilon)^ell}.
```

An arbitrarily inflated repetition or recurrence count is not covered by these upper recipes. With the actual full augmented dimension `2d`,

| Resource | Sufficient upper bound |
|---|---|
| Repetitions | `r<=C_r epsilon^-R` |
| Primitive factors | `N<=C_N epsilon^-R` |
| Recurrence ceiling | `Q<=C_Q epsilon^-(R+1)` |
| Actual physical duration | `T<=C_T epsilon^-P` |
| Inverse physical ramp width | `1/(t0 rho)<=C_rho epsilon^-(R+1)` |
| Target-grid candidates | `[8 kappa_0(d+1) A_alpha+5]^s_0 epsilon^-((nu+1)s_0)`, `A_alpha=64d Bsum` |
| Each of five recurrence searches | `C_Q^(2d) epsilon^(-2d(R+1))` candidates |
| Coupling search | `D+1` nodes; value-enclosure error `b/8` proportional to `epsilon^nu` |

The original body's exponents use `nu=D`; the separately checked readout improves them to `nu=k0`. All other fixed data and the `D+1` interpolation grid remain. The protected parent uses its larger recurrence ceiling with its Frobenius acceptance test. The different root parent's smaller ceiling/operator test must not be substituted. Exact positive **computable** durations include all recurrence waits and same-duration smoothing; rationalizing them needs separately charged error and phase/aging updates. Candidate counts do not bound arbitrary computable coefficient or matrix-oracle runtime. Tiny `a`, deep trees, large `d` or ill-conditioned Vandermonde data can give enormous constants. Varying these inputs with accuracy requires recomputing the powers.

## 6. Full positivity, scalar, calibration, work and moments

Each path bond `lambda(I-SWAP)` is positive with norm `2lambda`; its four Pauli coefficients, including scalar, have magnitude `lambda/2`, and incident added block-norm load is at most `4lambda`. Each positive port pulse has peak norm at most `2g`. Whole robust positivity needs a supplied peak-defect allowance `zeta_pk` and `R_s>=h+zeta_pk`; the integrated error allowance alone gives no such peak guarantee. Separate positivity of all old blocks requires a supplied literal decomposition and individual reserves, changing scalar, phase, norm and action.

For fixed reserve, the nominal full norm has the uniform bound `B_0=h+R_s+||J||+2g`. Distinct ledgers are

```
physical scalar rate=h0+R_s+lambda j0+g f(t),
added norm action<=(R_s+lambda||J||)(T+w)+2A_s,
extra scalar action=(R_s+lambda j0)(T+w)+A_s,
full norm action<=B_0(C_T+w)epsilon^-P,
port variation<=4g C_N epsilon^-R,
port peak slew<=3g C_rho epsilon^-(R+1).
```

Waits accrue static/path/reserve action even while the port is off. Norm action is not mean thermodynamic work. A sufficient constant full-generator error rate is `epsilon/[64(T+w)]`, whose inverse is at most `64(C_T+w)epsilon^-(P+1)`. A common pulse-time shift allowance `epsilon/(256gN)` can spend at most `epsilon/64` by the variation estimate. These are alternative allocations of the single total defect budget. Static strength error costs `abs(delta_lambda)||J||(T+w)`, including its scalar; a fixed relative hardware error is not free. Nominal oracle digits needed to evaluate long recurrence matrices are a separate cost.

For regular closed evolution with endpoint port control zero,

```
W_nom=Tr[(H+R_s I+lambda J)(rho_nom(T)-rho_0)],
abs(W_nom)<=min(4gN_active,2h+lambda||J||),
abs(W_act-W_nom)<=(h+lambda||J||/2)min(2,2E_int)
                  +||E(T)||+||E(0)||.
```

Endpoint defects therefore need their own allowances for a work comparison. No heat law, physical energy identification, actuator manufacture, installation/cooling/reset work or native clock is derived. For a retained observable with full norm `B_O`, trace error `e` yields mean, second-moment and variance errors at most `B_O e`, `B_O^2 e` and `3B_O^2 e`. A subsequent autonomous-clock/mediator construction adds factors and growing norms; its state supply, clock size, penalty, action, calibration and moments must be recomputed from this actual `T` and slew.

## 7. Parent, retained failures and publication boundary

The sole intended mathematical parent is the [quantitative positive-time compiler](CONDITIONED_POSITIVE_TIME_COMPILER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-15.md). The protected finite-target-grid proof and its exposed assessment supply the recipe used here; the parent's alternative proof remains historical scope, not an identification of constants or durations. The actual canonical parent is 97,212 bytes, SHA256 `db922c9b3f67a603961f5a621a67eea7fa4894b793befbcdd3b7b034011e540a`, published as regular OPEN PR 9622 at head `70676cfdaa37280254c95e55c8d550816daf0040` and attached. Its protected proof is the exact half-open interval `[39210,70080)` and exposed comparison is `[70233,97212)`. Their hashes are `dd6cca8552a117d97f7be21c7b999ecd2276382f6cc762954bd97d00e3a6ff04` and `227180a0822eab4e3dbfc002b6604d914af23589c29add9cca71e1a2f3ae2db0`. Actual source acceptance, wrapper review, canonical BODY_MAP and publication/attachment records are preserved in the parent binding. This parent publication does not publish the present claim or bind its own future Git base.

The counterexamples remain narrow: `p(z)=z-c` defeats arbitrary coupling selection; an identically-zero determinant fails this fixed certificate but is no general impossibility; high-order cancellation forbids unproved leading-term dominance; smaller `k0` does not remove higher-degree interpolation nodes. `H=cI-lambda_*J` can cancel a chosen path, and path evolution over time proportional to `1/lambda` is not negligible merely because `lambda` is small. Noncommuting `H` and `W` forbid reversing window order or replacing actual aging by a prescribed time. A narrow high terminal defect can have small integral but unbounded endpoint norm/work and can defeat positivity; an uncharged scalar affects coherent phase during long waits. No compiler initializes memory, erases retained records, cools a clock or guarantees reuse.

The assessment is source-exposed by the author of the parent protected proof and later comparison, using the same model/effort. Root described the interpolation route and sharpening before checking. There is no protected new interpolation derivation, independent-model replication, numerical run, coefficient example or external theorem lookup. The root readout and exposed majorants are attributed separately. Earlier read-only access failures are preserved as bookkeeping failures, not science. Full original bodies, source decisions and actual metadata receipts remain recoverable with narrow hash deduplication, not recursive publication archives.

