# Root self-read and sharper coefficient-index option

The immutable proposal6cae05fe was read completely after drafting. The D-exponent construction remains a sufficient upper recipe: D is a degree upper bound, not an asserted order of vanishing. Its finite Vandermonde selection avoids any exact zero decision or a requirement that lower-order coefficients be absent. The full finite-window chronology and complete error budget remain explicit. This is a root self-check, not independent acceptance.

A sharper option is already visible before the one deliberate weakening in equation(1): use b_Lambda=a*Lambda^k0/A_V, without replacing Lambda^k0 by the smaller Lambda^D. The same D+1-node grid, fixed enclosure accuracy b_Lambda/8, strict lower threshold b_Lambda/2 and singular-value bound then give kappa=K_cert*Lambda^(-k0). No assertion that k0 is the first nonzero coefficient is needed; interpolation isolates that coefficient regardless of all the others. Consequently replace the conditioning exponent D by k0 in the accuracy powers: R=ell*(2*k0+1), P=R+2*d*(R+1), target-grid count O(epsilon^(-(k0+1)*s)), coupling-value enclosure tolerance proportional to epsilon^k0. D remains in the number of coupling grid points and the fixed rational Vandermonde constants. This is a proposed strengthening to be checked separately, not retroactively part of the original frozen text.

No numerical determinant example, pulse search, scientific program or external theorem was used. Independent checking and acceptance of this new interpolation composition remain pending, as does final acceptance/publication of its quantitative compiler parent. Fixed Hamiltonian and time units, complete computable input matrices, chosen tree family and nonzero coefficient certificate are supplied. Physical suppliers and efficient scaling in plant size remain open.


