# Accuracy-scaled coupling: source-exposed analytic assessment

The frozen root construction 6cae05fe is supported as a conditional, finite-window, complete-output compiler with the supplied polynomial-tree certificate. Its coarse degree exponent is a sufficient upper recipe. The separately frozen root readout 899a28b9 also gives a valid sharpening: the conditioning exponent may be the supplied nonzero coefficient index k0, without asserting that any lower coefficient is zero. Neither result establishes a uniform theorem over varying certificates, an efficient compiler in qubit count, a native supplier, or a physical implementation. No mathematical repair to the frozen construction was needed in this assessment.

This is a source-exposed analytic check by the author of the fixed-certificate proof dd6cca85 and of comparison 227180a0, using the same selected model and effort. It is not a protected derivation of the interpolation route, an independent-model replication, or a retained audit. The new candidate, its readout and the task description were seen before this assessment was written. The optional sharpening originated in the root readout; the explicit uniform constants below are an exposed rederivation, not a new independent discovery.

The parent's source acceptance changed during this task. At first exposure it was pending; actual root decision 9f90d834, recorded at 21:00:28 UTC on 2026-10-15, now accepts the two qualified fixed-certificate recipes and explicitly excludes this accuracy-scaled proposal. The candidate's and readout's historical pending statements remain byte-identical. This report is a recommendation about the new proposal, not a claim that root has already accepted it or published it.

## 1. Exact scope, sources and inherited obligations

The principal immutable inputs are:

