The full changed argument, readout, source list, current parent decision and its metadata verifier were read. Complete earlier readings of dd6cca85, the earlier alternative 2de387eb, the old compiler bda0be88 and its separate review 3ad0ab65 remain valid at their exact identities. The affected target search, recurrence, smoothing, window and resource passages of dd6cca85 were reread here. SOURCE_MANIFEST.json records full identities, coverage and selectively deduplicated recovery members. The older parent source archives are not recursively copied.

The actual contract fixes a nonempty complete finite plant of dimension d>=2, its whole computable H including literal H0, its supplied positive ordinary-NN path J, a single supplied X/Y port, g and t0, and the full retained target W with a determinant phase lift. All fillers and all original factors belong to that plant. An arbitrary passive reference can be correlated with every factor. The augmented direct sum is mathematical bookkeeping, not a physical register or a discarded output.

In addition, the construction consumes one fixed finite list of bracket trees, a fixed finite polynomial-degree bound D, a certified nonzero coefficient lower bound, and uniform norm bounds. These are substantive quantitative inputs. Computability must cover the primitive nominal matrices and their polynomial coordinates, including the time/port parameters needed to evaluate them. A fixed computable Hilbert-Schmidt basis suffices; equivalently the supplied polynomial-coordinate data must be consistent with the supplied matrices. Merely naming an arbitrary noncomputable basis would not support the claimed searches. This is already implicit in the candidate's assertion that its entries are computable-coefficient polynomials; it is made explicit here as an input obligation, not an additional physical supplier.

All conditions from the accepted compiler remain: complete background and omitted-edge accounting, supplied isolation, actual timing and actual H aging, the phase lift, positive-port/scalar accounting, and the distinction between whole-generator positivity and separately positive old local channels. Memory reset consequences require their own premise on the actual aged input. No memory or pure controller state is supplied by this construction.

## 2. Polynomial certificate and what its existence means

For the five primitive matrices

    X_i(z) = diag(-i t0(Hbar+z Jbar+v_i), -i t0 Hbar),

every matrix entry is affine in z. A binary commutator with ell_l leaves is a finite sum of products of ell_l such entries, so its degree is at most ell_l. Every tree with at least two leaves has zero second block: at its lowest nontrivial bracket the identical second-block leaves commute, and every subsequent bracket containing that zero block remains zero. This is exact algebra over the whole plant, not a tolerance test.

With s=d^2-1 trees, each column of C(z) has degree at most its tree's leaf count. Each determinant term chooses one entry per column; hence D=sum_l ell_l is a valid degree upper bound. It need not equal the actual degree or the order of vanishing at zero. In a real orthonormal basis of skew-Hermitian traceless matrices the coefficients are real. They are computable by finite polynomial arithmetic from the supplied data.

A supplied certificate |a_k0|>=a>0 proves that this particular tree family's determinant is not identically zero. It makes no claim that k0 is minimal. Conversely, if this same fixed family has a certified nonzero determinant at a supplied rational z_star, at least one coefficient is nonzero. Approximating all finitely many coefficients with successively smaller certified intervals eventually finds one interval excluding zero. A positive rational lower bound then exists and can be returned. This terminates under that promise without identifying the first nonzero coefficient or deciding exact zeros. It has no supplied uniform oracle-time bound.

There is no circular inference from a desired target W to the basis certificate. The certificate concerns the actual augmented primitive family before target compilation. The old qualitative controllability result can justify the existence of some finite tree family at an admitted coupling; it does not produce the displayed conditioning constants for free. Since the derived algebra contains (su(d),0), finitely many commutator monomials of length at least two can be chosen at such a coupling. Once chosen, their entries remain the same polynomial family for all z. Finding and certifying that family remains a separate operation. The new proposal correctly consumes its result.

Uniform norm bounds also check. Repeatedly applying ||[A,B]||<=2||A||||B|| gives

    ||b_l(z)|| <= beta_l = 2^(ell_l-1) M^ell_l.

The Euclidean norm of its coordinate column equals ||b_l(z)||_F and is at most sqrt(d) beta_l. Therefore

    ||C(z)||_2 <= ||C(z)||_F
               <= sqrt(d) (sum_l beta_l^2)^(1/2)
               <= sqrt(d) Bsum <= U.

These are full-space bounds, uniform over z in [0,1]. Rational choices require no irrational equality decision: for example U=d Bsum is a sufficient rational choice when M is rational. Much smaller supplied certified U is also allowed.

## 3. A separate interpolation derivation and the strict search

Here is a Lagrange-polynomial derivation of the load-bearing estimate. Let the candidate's D+1 distinct rational nodes be x_j in [1/2,1), and define

    L_j(x) = product_(m != j) (x-x_m)/(x_j-x_m).

For q_Lambda(x)=p(Lambda x), exact interpolation gives

    q_Lambda(x) = sum_j p(Lambda x_j) L_j(x).

Extracting the coefficient of x^k0 yields

    a_k0 Lambda^k0 = sum_j w_j p(Lambda x_j),
    w_j = coefficient_(x^k0) L_j(x).

These rational w_j are exactly row k0 of the inverse Vandermonde matrix. Their absolute sum A_V is positive: the coefficient-extraction functional is nonzero, so its values on a basis cannot all vanish. Consequently

    max_j |p(Lambda x_j)| >= a Lambda^k0/A_V.            (A)

This identity explains why arbitrary lower-order coefficients and cancellations at individual nodes do not invalidate the result. No leading-term approximation is being used. It also shows that the grid need not know which node will work.

For uniform notation in the rest of this report, put

    nu = D       for the original frozen construction,
    nu = k0      for the separately proposed sharpening.

Since 0<Lambda<=1 and k0<=D, (A) gives a witness of magnitude at least

    b = a Lambda^nu/A_V

in either case. For a certified approximation p_hat_j with |p_hat_j-p_j|<=b/8, set L_j=|p_hat_j|-b/8. Then L_j<=|p_j|. At a witness with |p_j|>=b,

    L_j >= |p_j|-b/4 >= 3b/4 > b/2.

Thus the strict acceptance test L_j>b/2 has a fixed margin. Approximation to this one prescribed absolute accuracy at each node suffices. If the approximations are rational, the strict comparison itself is an exact rational comparison; failed candidates need no endless threshold refinement. All D+1 nodes are a finite candidate set, and at least one passes. The selected rational lambda obeys

    Lambda/2 <= lambda < Lambda,
    |det C(lambda)| > a Lambda^nu/(2 A_V).              (B)

The lower bound Lambda/2 is useful for describing the actual parameter family; the finite-window error only needs the upper bound. D continues to determine the grid size and the Vandermonde constants under the k0 sharpening. It cannot be replaced by k0 in those places unless additional degree information is separately established.

The case k0=0 is valid. The determinant enclosure tolerance may then be a fixed positive constant while the selected nodes move toward zero. The coefficient identity still holds and gives a uniform conditioning bound. Such a certificate is unavailable for families whose determinant actually vanishes at zero; the theorem does not assert otherwise.

## 4. Full singular-value and coordinate bounds

Write the s singular values of C(lambda) as sigma_1,...,sigma_s. Their product is |det C(lambda)|, and each is at most U. Hence

    sigma_min > a Lambda^nu/(2 A_V U^(s-1)).            (C)

For Z=sum_l c_l b_l(lambda), let z be its coordinate vector in the same Hilbert-Schmidt basis. Then

    ||c||_1 <= sqrt(s)||c||_2
             <= sqrt(s)||z||_2/sigma_min
             = sqrt(s)||Z||_F/sigma_min
             <= sqrt(sd)||Z||/sigma_min.

Therefore the required parent bound is supplied by

    kappa(Lambda) = K_cert Lambda^(-nu),
    K_cert >= max(1, 2 sqrt(sd) A_V U^(s-1)/a).

A rational majorant always suffices; replacing sqrt(sd) by sd is one explicit conservative rational choice. There is no missing reference-dimension factor and no use of an excitation-sector singular value. The only coordinate-space dimension here is s=d^2-1 for the complete plant. An arbitrary reference is handled later by the operator-to-channel estimate.

This verifies the exact quantitative premise imported from dd6cca85 at every selected coupling. It is a bound for the selected nodes, not for all lambda in [Lambda/2,Lambda]. A polynomial can have zeros in that interval; selection is essential.

## 5. Explicit uniform resource constants after parameter substitution

The big-O powers in the root proposal are correct for the specified sufficient recipe. To make the dependence checkable without treating lambda-dependent parent constants as fixed, the following constants give a direct substitution proof.

Keep the root's fixed rational L_win and set Lambda=epsilon/L_win, 0<epsilon<=1. For either choice of nu above define

    kappa_0 = K_cert L_win^nu,
    K_bar = 1 + s[4 kappa_0(d+1)+2],
    S_bar = K_bar Bsum.

For tree l let k_l be its elementary signed-word length and retain the parent's uniform Taylor bound

    a_l = (k_l M)^(ell_l+1)/(ell_l+1)! + beta_l^2/2.

These a_l are remainder constants, not determinant coefficients or the parent positive split weights. They are uniform in lambda because M and the tree list are uniform. Put

    C_bar = 2 K_bar^2 sum_l a_l,
    Q_word = 2 sum_l k_l,
    R = ell(2nu+1),
    C_r = 1 + 2K_bar + 8S_bar^2 + (16C_bar)^ell,
    C_N = Q_word C_r,
    C_Q = 1 + 512(2d) C_N,
    P = R + 2d(R+1),
    C_T = 2 t0 C_N C_Q^(2d),
    C_rho = 8C_r/t0 + 16g C_N.

The actual parent coefficient budget is

    K = 1+s[4 kappa_0(d+1)epsilon^(-nu)+2]
      <= K_bar epsilon^(-nu).

Thus S<=S_bar epsilon^(-nu) and C<=C_bar epsilon^(-2nu). In the selected repetition count

    r = ceil max{1,2K,8S^2/epsilon,(16C/epsilon)^ell},

the powers nu and 2nu+1 are at most R because ell>=2 and nu>=0. Since 2K>=2, the ceiling is bounded by one plus the sum of the last three terms, giving

    r <= C_r epsilon^(-R),
    N <= C_N epsilon^(-R).

The parent uses augmented dimension 2d, delta=epsilon/(16N), and Q=ceil(32(2d)/delta), so

    Q <= C_Q epsilon^(-(R+1)),
    T <= 2t0 N Q^(2d) <= C_T epsilon^(-P).              (D)

For rho=min{1/(8r),epsilon/(16t0gN)},

    1/(t0rho) <= C_rho epsilon^(-(R+1)).                (E)

These explicit constants are a rederivation in this exposed report. They introduce no new algorithm or lower-bound claim. The recipe must actually use the stated ceiling/max choice; an arbitrarily inflated repetition count is not covered by these upper powers. A shorter word may exist; no optimality is claimed.

The target-grid count also checks. With A_alpha=64d Bsum, its spacing is alpha=epsilon/A_alpha, radius is R0=4 kappa_0(d+1)epsilon^(-nu), and m_grid=ceil(R0/alpha)+1. Therefore

    (2m_grid+1)^s
      <= [8 kappa_0(d+1)A_alpha+5]^s
         epsilon^(-(nu+1)s).                            (F)

Each of the five recurrence searches has at most

    C_Q^(2d) epsilon^(-2d(R+1))

candidates. The coupling search has exactly the bounded set of D+1 candidate nodes and requires determinant value accuracy b/8 proportional to epsilon^nu. These are counts and enclosure tolerances, not classical runtime bounds for arbitrary computable coefficient oracles.

The recurrence bound is uniform in lambda. The torus-box argument applies to any complete 2d-dimensional skew-Hermitian spectrum, including degeneracies and arbitrarily close frequencies. It requires no spectral gap, continuity of the selected recurrence integer, or shared recurrence period across different accuracies. The parent's larger Q and Frobenius acceptance test must remain together. Its actual durations are positive computable numbers: selected grid weights are rational, positive roots determine small word times, and inverse replacements have durations t0(2q_i-u). The exact total T includes every wait. The new coupling search does not silently convert this into the distinct root recipe with rationally rounded durations. Implemented timing approximations must still be charged.

For clarity, the original body's exponents are R=ell(2D+1), P=R+2d(R+1), and target count power (D+1)s. The readout's optional exponents are R=ell(2k0+1), P=R+2d(R+1), and target count power (k0+1)s. Both keep all polynomial/Vandermonde/tree constants fixed. Neither is uniform if the supplied degree, coefficient lower bound, conditioning certificate, target-access model, dimension, time unit, port strength or window grows with accuracy.

## 6. Actual aging, full output, finite window and scalar phase

At the selected lambda, dd6cca85 constructs an augmented word whose first block approximates the traceless target and whose second block approximates I, while the second block is exactly exp(-iT Hbar) for its actual positive duration T. Its signed approximation, positive recurrence replacement, target-grid approximation and smoothing bounds are uniform once the quantitative input above is inserted. Their separate constants give the inherited final operator bound 15epsilon/32. There is no assumption lambda T is small.

Restoring the physical scalar and then allowing a zero-port-control window gives the correct comparator

    V_s = exp(-i chi(T+s)) exp(-isH) W exp(-iTH),
    chi(T+s) = (R_s+lambda j0)(T+s) + A_s + theta,
    A_s = g sum_active(t_l-t0rho),
    0 <= s <= w.

The window comparator is not W exp(-i(T+s)H) in general. Literal H0 and the scalar h0 inside H occur in the actual background factors; h0 is not dropped or added again to chi. The physical identity coefficient is h0+R_s+lambda j0+g f(t). The extra scalar phase uses actual T+s, the smoothed area A_s and the supplied phase lift theta. A channel is insensitive to global phase, but the stated coherent operator comparison keeps it explicitly.

Using Duhamel only during the post-endpoint window,

    ||U_nom(T+s)-V_s|| <= 15epsilon/32+lambda||Jbar||s.

The choice L_win>=max(1,64 b_bar(1+w_bar)) ensures, without division by a possibly zero b_bar or w,

    lambda||Jbar||w <= epsilon b_bar w/L_win <= epsilon/64.

Let E_int be the integral of the full actual-minus-nominal generator norm over [0,T+w]. If E_int<=epsilon/64, the complete operator difference is at most epsilon/2. For every joint plant/reference input rho, expanding the two conjugations gives

    ||(U_act tensor I)rho(U_act* tensor I)
      -(V_s tensor I)rho(V_s* tensor I)||_1
      <= 2||U_act-V_s|| <= epsilon.                     (G)

This is unhalved trace distance, uniformly over the whole interval. No reference-dimension factor, partial trace, initialization of fillers, diagonal-input restriction or selected excitation sector is used. A supplied full input-state error adds once by contractivity and must have its own allocation if the total desired error is epsilon. The bound does not imply a smaller error against an unaged input, nor does it establish a memory premise merely from a one-site marginal.

For a finite product of compiler targets the parent qualification remains necessary: compose augmented pairs and accumulate their errors before reconstructing total actual H aging. Multiplying separately reconstructed bare endpoint formulas would insert intermediate H evolutions between target factors. The present candidate directly compiles one complete W using the finite grid, so it does not require a new multi-factor composition theorem. Any later use of that optional consequence must keep the same baseline H and its actual aging.

Design and finite searches occur before the declared physical timeline. If the actual plant evolves during that design, the additional evolution requires a separately supplied chronological contract. T is produced by the compiler and is not prescribed in advance. The finite-window result allows observation throughout [T,T+w]; it is not permanent stopping, an absorbing final state or controller reuse.

## 7. Positive channels, calibration, action, work and moments

The static path and port remain supplied ordinary-NN and onsite positive blocks. On the accepted path each bond lambda(I-SWAP) has norm 2lambda and its four Pauli coefficients, including its scalar, have magnitude lambda/2. The incident added block-norm load is at most 4lambda. The pulse is C(t)=g f(t)(I+sigma P)>=0, with f a cubic-ramped profile, zero endpoint value and derivative, peak norm at most 2g, and unchanged duration T. No added NN edge, global control channel, auxiliary vacuum or pure clock is hidden in this step.

With a fixed supplied peak-fault bound zeta_pk and reserve R_s>=h+zeta_pk, the actual whole generator is positive. If only nominal positivity is required, R_s>=h suffices. A bound on E_int alone does not imply either a peak bound or positivity. Whole-generator positivity does not make every literal old local term positive. A stronger positive-local-block contract requires a supplied decomposition H=sum H_alpha with individual reserves r_alpha>=||H_alpha|| and any fault allocation, changing total scalar, norm, phase and action. It can retain the accuracy powers if those new reserves are fixed, but it is an additional supplied interface and bookkeeping obligation.

For fixed reserve, the nominal full norm is bounded uniformly by

    B_0 = h+R_s+||J||+2g,

since lambda<=1. Equations (D)-(E) give explicit sufficient bounds

    control variation <= 4g C_N epsilon^(-R),
    control peak slew <= 3g C_rho epsilon^(-(R+1)),
    full norm action <= B_0(C_T+w)epsilon^(-P).

The more informative action ledgers remain

    added norm action <= (R_s+lambda||J||)(T+w)+2A_s,
    extra scalar action = (R_s+lambda j0)(T+w)+A_s.

They must not be replaced by pulse count alone. Long recurrence waits accrue old-background, path and reserve action even when the port is off. Smaller lambda need not make lambda T small. If hardware specifies a common cap on total action or maximum duration, this theorem does not establish that cap.

A sufficient constant full-generator error rate is epsilon/[64(T+w)]. Its inverse is bounded by

    64(C_T+w)epsilon^(-(P+1)).

This is a sufficient precision recipe, not a lower bound on the accuracy required by every possible compiler. A conservative common timing shift |Delta t|<=epsilon/(256gN) gives integrated pulse discrepancy at most epsilon/64 using the full variation; its inverse tolerance has sufficient power R+1. Observation-time changes must either update H aging and chi or be separately charged using complete generator and target-time bounds. Exact computable durations are nominal data, not a proof of a native clock with exact timing.

These are alternative uses of one total E_int budget. If several calibration, timing, coefficient and omitted-edge errors occur together, their integrated upper bounds must sum to at most epsilon/64; each cannot independently consume the entire allowance while retaining (G).

For a static path-strength error delta_lambda, the full error budget includes |delta_lambda| ||J|| (T+w), including its scalar effect. Thus selecting lambda of order epsilon does not permit an unpriced fixed relative hardware error. Using the conservative duration upper recipe, an absolute allowance of order epsilon^(P+1), and correspondingly a relative allowance of order epsilon^P when ||J||>0, is sufficient. This statement gives a possible conservative allocation; it does not assert that the actual selected run saturates the duration bound. Norm errors in H, other local coefficients, unintended boundary interactions and pulse defects are likewise included in E_int.

Nominal evaluation accuracy is a separate issue. For example, evaluating exp(2qX_i) to a required error entails matrix data accurate enough for that q, by Duhamel. The recurrence candidate count does not erase that cost. A supplied computable oracle eventually returns the necessary certified digits; this report claims no runtime bound on doing so. No coupling grid, target grid or recurrence search has actually been executed here.

For regular closed-system dynamics, with controls zero at the endpoints, the formal mean-work identity remains

    W_nom = Tr[(H+R_s I+lambda J)(rho_nom(T)-rho_0)],
    |W_nom| <= min(4gN_active, 2h+lambda||J||).

Consequently nominal mean work has a bounded sufficient estimate even while duration, variation and norm action grow. This is an endpoint cancellation, not a free actuator or an identification of norm action with thermodynamic work. For the same initial state and a regular actual defect E, the inherited endpoint comparison is

    |W_act-W_nom| <= (h+lambda||J||/2) min(2,2E_int)
                    +||E(T)||+||E(0)||.

Thus a small integrated dynamical defect does not by itself give a small work discrepancy. Endpoint defect allowances or a separately priced variation estimate remain necessary. No bath, heat law, microscopic energy mapping, control-source energy, cooling or reset cost is derived.

For any declared retained observable of norm B_O, a complete state error e gives mean error <=B_O e, second-moment error <=B_O^2 e and variance error <=3B_O^2 e. For this external family a fixed full Hamiltonian norm makes those particular endpoint estimates uniform. A later autonomous clock or mediator substitution generally introduces growing norms and new state-supply premises. It must recompute clock size, penalty, action, calibration and moments from the new T and slew; the bounded external norm cannot be inherited without that calculation.

## 8. Failure routes and finite qualifications preserved

1. A nonzero coefficient does not make an arbitrary chosen coupling good. Algebraically p(z)=z-c has a certified nonzero linear coefficient but vanishes at c. The physical cancellation witness from the old compiler is H=cI-lambda_*J on a plant with more than the port, evaluated at lambda=lambda_*: the path cancels and port-only control cannot generate the full plant algebra. Choosing a sufficiently large c is compatible with whole positivity. The finite node selection, rather than an arbitrary weak-coupling assertion, addresses this issue.

2. If all coefficients of this particular determinant vanish, the supplied certificate fails. That says nothing universal about other tree families, other control constructions or the physical plant. Searching for a different family is a separate task. Conversely, an unspecified nonzero determinant obtained from a tree list that changes with accuracy does not provide the fixed-family constants used here.

3. The interpolation estimate needs no claim that k0 is the first nonzero coefficient. Replacing it by a leading-term dominance argument without controlling lower coefficients would be invalid. Replacing D+1 by k0+1 nodes merely because the exponent improved would also lack justification: higher-degree terms remain present.

4. Removing the path dynamically for the whole long preparation because lambda is small is invalid. Even lambda(I-SWAP) at time pi/(2lambda) has a nontrivial unitary of order-one distance from the identity. The actual compiler handles the path throughout its augmented recurrences; Duhamel is used only for the bounded final window and declared defects. There is no lambda T smallness premise.

5. The endpoint target cannot be read as W acting after a prescribed or zero aging time. Nor may exp(-isH) W be exchanged with W exp(-isH) without a commutation premise. The earlier finite X/Z ordering witness is retained by the parent comparison. These are comparator mistakes, not counterexamples to (G).

6. Small integrated error alone does not bound its peak or endpoint. A defect of height M supported on an interval of width epsilon/(64M) can meet the integral budget while its endpoint norm is M; choosing its sign can also defeat an unreserved positivity claim. A constant uncharged scalar defect changes the coherent phase over long waits even when its channel action is trivial. Actual calibration, positivity and work therefore have distinct contracts.

7. Fixed dimension does not fix arbitrary certificate discovery or oracle complexity. Tiny a, a poorly conditioned Vandermonde matrix, deep trees and a large dimension can make the constants enormous. If those data or the requested window vary with epsilon, the displayed exponents must be recomputed. No practical efficiency, common hardware caps or native supplier follows from a polynomial inverse-tolerance upper recipe.

8. A full-output conditional unitary compiler does not initialize a reservoir, cool a clock, certify an aged memory state, reset a dirty filler, erase a record, or guarantee reuse. Those tasks require their own complete input-state and dynamical contracts. None is imported by this proposal.

These failures are narrowly scoped. They are not a no-go theorem, a claim that no other compiler can improve the bounds, or evidence against the stated selected-coupling construction.

