## 10. Actual evidence and limits

No scientific program, numerical fixture, polynomial-coefficient example, target-grid search, recurrence search, pulse simulation or external theorem lookup was run. The argument was checked analytically. In particular the finite search counts were not converted into fictitious executed test counts. There is no claim that hashes or metadata receipts prove mathematics.

The local helpers capture selected exact sources, verify their identities/recovery, check the relevant immutable seals and actual historical receipt linkage, and seal this report. Their actual subprocess records are under metadata_runs; each identifies its real argv, source at launch, stream hashes, timestamps, exit and timeout. The source-at-launch record for the current parent acceptance is the actual file named in its EXECUTION.json; no LAUNCH.json was invented. Selected receipt streams and their real recorder are recoverable once per hash. SEAL_OPERATION.json describes the direct in-process sealing operation rather than inventing another subprocess.

Two preliminary read-only shell probes failed: one acceptance read used a misspelled renewal directory, and one wc glob matched the still-empty output directory. ACCESS_FAILURES.md preserves their exact observed command/error/exit information. Both were access/bookkeeping failures, not scientific failures; the acceptance was subsequently read from its correct path. No metadata check failure or theorem failure is inferred from them.

The current source manifest and verification record state the precise coverage. The parent proof and earlier comparison are reused only at verified bytes; source recovery is selective rather than a recursive archive. All original proofs and readouts remain immutable. No W/C checkout, Git ref, PR, audit, checkpoint, lock, physical axiom or editable prompt file was changed. The selected model and effort were retained, and no subagent was spawned. Formal root disposition and any publication work remain separate from this frozen analytical assessment.
